.nh
.TH "PB-PREVIEW-STOP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-stop - Stop a temporary preview


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview stop <preview> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop a temporary preview

.PP
Stop the selected temporary preview's active forwarding. Other previews and durable tunnels remain separate resources.

.PP
A preview exposes a local target through a temporary Paperboat URL or private/team access policy. Inspect its status before sharing the URL, and stop or delete it when no longer needed. Browser HTTP terminates TLS at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for stop

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the stopped canonical preview resource as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
